      <h2>Author bio — short (50 words)</h2>
      <p>Njintieuh Sieni is a Cameroonian-born author based in Florida. Raised on stories told aloud, he writes epic fantasy rooted in African cosmology and oral tradition. <em>Blood of the Seven</em> is his debut novel and the first book of <em>The Seven Kingdoms of K'Thari</em>, a planned twelve-book saga.</p>

      <h2>Author bio — long</h2>
      {{ author.intro | md | safe }}
      <p>Before novels, he made music and designed clothing, drafting the stories that would become K'Thari all along. He moved to the United States in 2010 and now lives and writes in Florida. He published independently and built the saga piece by piece — manuscript, maps, art and covers — and his long-term ambition is to bring K'Thari to the screen.</p>

      <h2>Interview topics</h2>
